## Original Content
Over the years, you’ve probably heard at least a few people casually describe themselves as Epicureans. As used today, the label can refer to as little as enjoying the occasional expensive restaurant meal. The bar was a bit higher in the second century, as explained by ancient-history YouTuber Garrett Ryan in the new video above [&#8230;]

## Summary
This article discusses how the term 'Epicurean' is commonly used today to describe someone who enjoys fine dining, but in the second century, it referred to a more profound philosophical doctrine. A YouTuber named Garrett Ryan explains this contrast in a video.

## Key Points
- Modern usage of 'Epicurean' often implies a casual enjoyment of expensive meals.
- In the second century, Epicureanism was a rigorous ancient philosophy with deeper ethical meanings.
- Garrett Ryan, an ancient-history YouTuber, provides an explanation of this evolution in a video.


